Alex: Quick sync — I opened a PR to add migration examples for function-calling -> structured outputs. Need eyes on the JSON schema example and SDK snippet links: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3421 :eyes:
Maria: Looking now. Main question: do we prefer `response_shape` or `output_schema` in examples?
Alex: We standardized on `response_shape` in the SDK docs last quarter but older pages use `output_schema`. PR updates both, opts for response_shape to avoid churn.
Sam: Can we include a tiny fallback parsing example showing how to handle truncated or extra-text responses? e.g.:
```js
try {
  const parsed = JSON.parse(response);
} catch (e) {
  // fallback: regex capture of JSON blob
  const match = response.match(/\{.*\}/s);
  const parsed = match ? JSON.parse(match[0]) : { _raw: response };
}
```
Maria: Yes add that. Also add a one-liner curl for local testing: `curl -X POST https://api.redwood.com/v1/llm -d '{"prompt":"...","response_shape": {...}}' -H 'Authorization: Bearer $REDWOOD_KEY'`
DocBot: FYI — docs-lint reported a missing required `id` field in the tool example block; filed issue #88 and flagged the PR.
Kevin: I'll push a follow-up commit to add `id` on the tool examples and fix a couple of anchor links that were 404ing (schema-guides.md#tool-calling).
Nora: Also please include the Python SDK snippet — only JS was in the draft. Minimal example is fine to start.
Alex: Good call — added a concise Python snippet and updated the PR description with before/after screenshots for the rendered schema examples.
Sam: Quick review done, left inline comments on wording and a suggestion to reorder keys in the `response_shape` to match generator examples (predictability for newer readers).
Maria: LGTM once Kevin's `id` fix lands and the lint warnings are resolved. Can we merge after CI?
Alex: Yes, I'll merge after CI green. Thanks a lot for the fast reviews :tada:
DocBot: CI passed and PR merged by Alex — release note queued (internal changelog entry: "docs: migration examples + SDK snippets for response_shape and parsing fallbacks").
